{title: 503 - A Quiet Place}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #503 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 503}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]There is a [Bdim]quiet place,
[Am]Far from the [E/G#]rapid [C]pace where God [F]can soothe [Em]my [Am]troubled [Dm]mind.
[Dm]Sheltered [G]by [Dm]tree [F/C]and [C]flow'r,
[F]There in my [C]quiet [Dm]hour with Him [Gm/A#]my cares [C/G]are left [B7]behind.
[Em]Whether [Dm]a [C]garden small,
[C]Or [Em/B]on a mountain [Am]tall, [E/G#]New [C]strength and courage [F]there [Am/E]I [Em]find;
[Am]Then from [C/G]this [Am]quiet place
[Am]I [F]go prepared [Em]to face [Dm/A]a new [A7]day [Am]With [Dm]love [G#]for [G7]all mankind.
{end_of_verse}
